[2026-07-19T14:08:36.760Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=305c4f15b5fb4e034791c9201adfd5f5] Topic: Establish design tokens for colors, typography, spacing, and shadows
[2026-07-19T14:08:36.760Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=305c4f15b5fb4e034791c9201adfd5f5]   Trigger:   The project needed a consistent visual foundation before building out any real UI, replacing the generic default styling that shipped with the starter template.
[2026-07-19T14:08:36.760Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=305c4f15b5fb4e034791c9201adfd5f5]   Response:  - Reworked `app/globals.css` to define a full token set (primary/neutral/semantic colors, spacing scale, border radius, shadow levels, font sizes, and line heights) wired into Tailwind CSS v4 through the `@theme inline` block.
- Added reusable typography utility classes (heading and body text styles) built on top of the new font-size and line-height tokens.
- Swapped the default fonts in `app/layout.tsx` from Geist to Inter (body) and JetBrains Mono (monospace), updating the CSS variable names accordingly.
[2026-07-19T14:08:36.760Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=305c4f15b5fb4e034791c9201adfd5f5]   Decisions: - **Token-driven theming with Tailwind v4**: Colors, spacing, radius, and shadows were centralized as CSS variables mapped into Tailwind's theme layer rather than hard-coding values in components, making future rebranding or white-labeling a matter of editing one file instead of hunting through every component.
- **Font swap to Inter/JetBrains Mono**: The default Geist fonts were replaced to better match the intended brand voice and improve readability for a product-facing tool, at the cost of a small increase in bundle/font-loading complexity.
[2026-07-19T14:08:36.760Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=305c4f15b5fb4e034791c9201adfd5f5] Topic: Build core reusable UI component library (Button, Card, Input, Select, Tag, Alert)
[2026-07-19T14:08:36.760Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=305c4f15b5fb4e034791c9201adfd5f5]   Trigger:   Pages needed consistent, reusable building blocks instead of one-off styled markup, so a shared component set was created to match the new design tokens.
[2026-07-19T14:08:36.760Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=305c4f15b5fb4e034791c9201adfd5f5]   Response:  - Created `components/Button.tsx` supporting primary/secondary/ghost/icon variants, three sizes, disabled states, and an `asChild` mode for wrapping links.
- Created `components/Card.tsx`, `components/Input.tsx`, and `components/Select.tsx` with configurable shadow/padding, label/helper-text/error states, and consistent focus styling driven by the new tokens.
- Created `components/Tag.tsx` and `components/Alert.tsx` with multiple semantic variants (success, warning, error, info, purple, default) and optional dismiss/remove actions, and exposed all six components through a single `components/index.ts` barrel file.
[2026-07-19T14:08:36.760Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=305c4f15b5fb4e034791c9201adfd5f5]   Decisions: - **Hand-built lightweight component set over a third-party UI library**: A small custom set of components was written directly against the new tokens rather than adopting an external component library, keeping the bundle lean and giving full control over variant naming and styling to match the brand exactly.
- **Consistent variant/size pattern across components**: Every component follows the same `variant`/`size`/`className` prop shape so that future components can be added predictably and developers only need to learn the pattern once.
[2026-07-19T14:08:36.760Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=305c4f15b5fb4e034791c9201adfd5f5] Topic: Add design system showcase page and redesign homepage with new components
[2026-07-19T14:08:36.760Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=305c4f15b5fb4e034791c9201adfd5f5]   Trigger:   With tokens and components in place, the team needed a living reference page to see every style and component together, plus an updated homepage that reflects the new visual identity instead of the leftover starter-template content.
[2026-07-19T14:08:36.760Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=305c4f15b5fb4e034791c9201adfd5f5]   Response:  - Added `app/design-system/page.tsx`, a full showcase covering design principles, color swatches, typography scale, button variants, form fields, tags, alerts, spacing, and shadow levels, all built from the new shared components.
