[2026-07-19T14:12:42.279Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=416b3d14c2fed651df44e2115dc1fcc1] === Summary content (2 topics) ===
[2026-07-19T14:12:42.279Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=416b3d14c2fed651df44e2115dc1fcc1] Topic: Build Shopify Theme Builder design system with tokens and component library
[2026-07-19T14:12:42.279Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=416b3d14c2fed651df44e2115dc1fcc1]   Trigger:   The user provided a UI reference image and asked to implement the app's design system so the interface would move beyond the default starter-template styling.
[2026-07-19T14:12:42.279Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=416b3d14c2fed651df44e2115dc1fcc1]   Response:  - Reworked the global stylesheet to define a full token set (primary/neutral/semantic colors, spacing scale, border radius, shadow levels, font sizes and line heights) wired into Tailwind CSS v4, plus reusable heading/body typography utility classes.
- Swapped the default fonts from Geist to Inter (body) and JetBrains Mono (monospace) in the root layout to better match the intended visual identity.
- Built six shared components (Button, Card, Input, Select, Tag, Alert) with consistent variant/size/className prop patterns, exported through a single barrel file, and used them to build a new design-system showcase page plus a redesigned homepage with hero, features, and supported-pages sections.
[2026-07-19T14:12:42.279Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=416b3d14c2fed651df44e2115dc1fcc1]   Decisions: - **Token-driven theming over hard-coded styles**: colors, spacing, radius, and shadows were centralized as CSS variables mapped into Tailwind's theme layer instead of scattering values across components, so future rebranding only requires editing one file.
- **Hand-built component set instead of a third-party UI library**: a small custom library was written directly against the new tokens to keep the bundle lean and give full control over styling and naming, rather than adopting an external design system.
- **Dedicated living style guide**: a design-system route was added so anyone can verify visual consistency directly in the running app as new components are built, instead of relying on static documentation that can drift out of sync.
[2026-07-19T14:12:42.279Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=416b3d14c2fed651df44e2115dc1fcc1] Topic: Rewrite AGENTS.md into full engineering guidelines for the theme builder
[2026-07-19T14:12:42.279Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=416b3d14c2fed651df44e2115dc1fcc1]   Trigger:   The project needed a comprehensive reference document defining the product scope, tech stack, architecture, and engineering rules for AI agents working on the Shopify Theme Builder, replacing the generic placeholder notes left from the starter template.
[2026-07-19T14:12:42.279Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=416b3d14c2fed651df44e2115dc1fcc1]   Response:  - Replaced the minimal starter-template notice in AGENTS.md with a detailed specification covering the product's core flow (prompt to generated storefront to Shopify export), the required tech stack (Next.js, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, an AI provider layer, InsForge, Jolli, ImageKit, CodeRabbit), and a 10-step implementation workflow agents must follow.
- Documented architectural layering rules (UI, AI, Builder, Images, Database, Memory, Shopify) and a provider-agnostic AI interface for project plans, page streaming, selection edits, and Shopify section generation.
- Added detailed rules for stable section/element IDs and scoped inline editing, preview sandboxing and security constraints, Shopify ZIP export structure and validation, ImageKit asset handling, and testing/coding standards.
[2026-07-19T14:12:42.279Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=416b3d14c2fed651df44e2115dc1fcc1]   Decisions: - **Provider-independent AI layer**: the document mandates that all AI providers implement a shared interface and that model/provider selection come from environment variables, so the app is not locked into a single AI vendor and providers can be swapped without touching business logic.
- **Scoped patches over full-page regeneration**: inline edits must apply as structured, targeted operations tied to stable element IDs rather than regenerating entire pages, prioritizing speed and predictability for the editing experience and enabling reliable undo/revision history.
- **Sandboxed, schema-validated preview**: generated storefront code is treated as untrusted and must be rendered in a sandboxed iframe or schema-based renderer with strict restrictions (no eval, no arbitrary scripts, no exposed secrets), trading some flexibility for safety since the content originates from an AI model.
