[2026-07-19T17:50:40.574Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c23a8183d60dd57f04cad5fb8c837088] Topic: Add persistent header and sidebar navigation to app layout
[2026-07-19T17:50:40.574Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c23a8183d60dd57f04cad5fb8c837088]   Trigger:   The app previously rendered pages with no shared navigation chrome, so every page had to stand alone without a consistent way to move between sections or access account actions.
[2026-07-19T17:50:40.574Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c23a8183d60dd57f04cad5fb8c837088]   Response:  - Created a new Header component showing the product logo, a settings icon, and sign in/sign up buttons, fixed to the top of the viewport.
- Created a new Sidebar component listing Home, Projects, and Inspiration links, highlighting the active route based on the current path, fixed to the left edge below the header.
- Updated the root layout in app/layout.tsx to wrap all page content with the Header and Sidebar and added matching padding/margin so page content no longer sits underneath the fixed elements.
[2026-07-19T17:50:40.574Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c23a8183d60dd57f04cad5fb8c837088]   Decisions: - **Fixed positioning for header and sidebar**: both elements stay pinned on screen while content scrolls underneath, giving users constant access to navigation and account controls regardless of page length.
- **Icon library choice**: the lucide-react icon set was added as a dependency to supply consistent iconography (settings, navigation icons) across the new header and sidebar.
[2026-07-19T17:50:40.574Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c23a8183d60dd57f04cad5fb8c837088] Topic: Redesign home page around AI prompt input and template cards
[2026-07-19T17:50:40.574Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c23a8183d60dd57f04cad5fb8c837088]   Trigger:   The home page previously showed a generic feature list and supported-pages grid, which didn't reflect the product's core interaction of describing a page to an AI and getting a generated Shopify template.
[2026-07-19T17:50:40.574Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c23a8183d60dd57f04cad5fb8c837088]   Response:  - Rewrote app/page.tsx as a client component centered on a hero headline, a subtitle explaining the prompt-to-template flow, and a prominent input box with a send button for describing the desired page.
- Added a grid of clickable template starter cards (landing page, product page, cart page, collection page) each with an icon, title, and short description to give users quick starting points.
- Added a promotional banner section at the bottom referencing Shopify branding and the "idea to live store" pitch, using a Shopify logo image asset.
[2026-07-19T17:50:40.574Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c23a8183d60dd57f04cad5fb8c837088]   Decisions: - **Prompt-first layout over feature list**: the page now leads with an interactive input rather than marketing copy, putting the core AI-generation action front and center for first-time visitors.
- **Curated template suggestions**: a fixed set of common Shopify page types (landing, product, cart, collection) was chosen to guide users toward supported use cases instead of leaving the prompt box entirely open-ended.
