[2026-07-20T19:52:36.652Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=b10163ce56710bd9c030bc87262ee8a6] === Pipeline completed in 36.2s ===
[2026-07-20T19:52:36.652Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=b10163ce56710bd9c030bc87262ee8a6] === Summary content (2 topics) ===
[2026-07-20T19:52:36.652Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=b10163ce56710bd9c030bc87262ee8a6] Topic: Inline editing mode for generated page previews
[2026-07-20T19:52:36.652Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=b10163ce56710bd9c030bc87262ee8a6]   Trigger:   The user wanted an in-place editing experience for generated pages: an Edit button that turns on a mode where hovering a section shows a highlighted border and a floating popover offering text editing, AI-assisted edits, image changes, style controls, duplication, reordering, and deletion, with all changes reflected immediately in the live preview.
[2026-07-20T19:52:36.652Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=b10163ce56710bd9c030bc87262ee8a6]   Response:  - Added a new in-preview editing runtime that runs entirely inside the sandboxed preview frame (since the surrounding app cannot reach into it directly), providing hover highlighting, a floating toolbar of edit actions, and dedicated panels for text editing, styling, image replacement, AI prompts, and delete confirmation.
- Updated the preview shell logic to inject this runtime, listen for edit-mode toggling, and automatically re-enable editing behavior whenever the page content is refreshed.
- Added a page-update function in the builder's shared state that re-validates edited content through the same safety pipeline used for AI-generated pages and saves just the affected page after a short pause, and added an Edit/Done toggle button plus message handling in the preview component to receive edits and AI requests from the frame without them bouncing back and resetting it.
[2026-07-20T19:52:36.652Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=b10163ce56710bd9c030bc87262ee8a6]   Decisions: - **All editing logic lives inside the preview frame**: because the preview runs in a locked-down sandbox that the main app cannot reach into directly, every hover state, highlight, and edit action had to be built to run inside that frame and communicate outward through simple messages, rather than having the app manipulate the page content directly.
- **AI-assisted edits reuse the existing scoped-edit chat flow**: instead of building a separate pipeline for AI-driven inline changes, prompts entered in the popover are routed through the same targeted-edit mechanism already used elsewhere in the builder, keeping the feature simpler at the cost of it feeling like a normal chat request under the hood.
- **AI image generation is stubbed through the text pipeline for now**: real AI-generated or AI-transformed images depend on an image-generation service that isn't connected in this project yet, so that option currently sends the request through the same text-based edit flow as a temporary placeholder.
[2026-07-20T19:52:36.652Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=b10163ce56710bd9c030bc87262ee8a6]   Todo:      Wire up real AI image generation (needs an image-generation service integration) instead of routing image requests through the text-edit pipeline.
[2026-07-20T19:52:36.652Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=b10163ce56710bd9c030bc87262ee8a6] Topic: Bigger, draggable, in-place toolbar with per-element selection
[2026-07-20T19:52:36.652Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=b10163ce56710bd9c030bc87262ee8a6]   Trigger:   After trying the new editing mode, the user asked for a larger popover toolbar positioned inside the highlighted area (not floating above it) that could be dragged if needed, and pointed out that only whole sections could be selected — individual pieces inside a section, like a heading or button, couldn't be targeted for editing on their own.
[2026-07-20T19:52:36.652Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=b10163ce56710bd9c030bc87262ee8a6]   Response:  - Enlarged the floating toolbar's buttons, icons, spacing, and shadow, and scaled up the accompanying editing panels to match, making the controls easier to see and tap.
- Changed the toolbar's positioning so it anchors inside the top-right corner of the highlighted area (clamped to stay on-screen) instead of floating above it, keeping it reachable even for content near the top of the page.
- Added a drag handle so the toolbar can be repositioned anywhere and will stay put once moved, and reworked the hover-selection logic so the deepest element under the cursor (a heading, button, image, etc.) becomes the edit target rather than always selecting the entire surrounding section; duplicate, move, delete, style, and AI actions now all operate on that specific inner element.
[2026-07-20T19:52:36.652Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=b10163ce56710bd9c030bc87262ee8a6]   Decisions: - **Granular, cursor-driven element selection over section-only selection**: rather than always treating an entire section as the unit of editing, hovering now targets whichever specific element the pointer is over, letting users edit a single heading or button directly at the cost of more complex logic for detecting what's under the cursor.
- **Toolbar anchored inside the target instead of floating above it**: pinning the toolbar to the target's own top-right corner (rather than positioning it outside the highlighted area) guarantees it stays visible and reachable even for sections at the very top of the page, trading a small amount of visual overlap with the content for reliable accessibility.
