[2026-07-22T03:28:24.515Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=4fdef5ef13c82a0ab42e20e8b21a372c] === Summary content (3 topics) ===
[2026-07-22T03:28:24.515Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=4fdef5ef13c82a0ab42e20e8b21a372c] Topic: Add Projects page with grid of cards and auto-captured thumbnails
[2026-07-22T03:28:24.515Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=4fdef5ef13c82a0ab42e20e8b21a372c]   Trigger:   The user wanted clicking "Projects" in the sidebar to open a page listing every project they've created, each shown as a card with a preview thumbnail, an automatically generated title, and the creation date, laid out in a grid.
[2026-07-22T03:28:24.515Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=4fdef5ef13c82a0ab42e20e8b21a372c]   Response:  - Built a new Projects page that fetches all of the signed-in user's projects, sorted newest first, and renders them in a responsive 1/2/3-column card grid with loading, error, and empty states (the empty state includes a "Create a project" call to action).
- Each card shows a cropped 16:10 thumbnail, a cleaned-up auto-derived title, and a formatted creation date, and links to that project's editor.
- Improved the existing prompt-to-title logic to strip filler lead-ins like "Create a…" or "Build me a…" and capitalize the result, so titles read naturally instead of echoing the raw prompt; added `listProjects()` and `saveProjectThumbnail()` to support the page.
[2026-07-22T03:28:24.515Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=4fdef5ef13c82a0ab42e20e8b21a372c]   Decisions: - **Client-side, best-effort capture over a server-side screenshot service**: thumbnails are rasterized in the browser by reusing the existing "Export to PNG" offscreen-iframe technique rather than standing up a server-side rendering/screenshot pipeline, keeping the feature self-contained and avoiding new infrastructure.
- **Never block generation on thumbnail success**: capture and upload failures are swallowed and simply leave a "Preview generating…" placeholder, so a broken thumbnail pipeline can never interrupt the core page-generation flow.
- **Deterministic title derivation instead of an extra AI call**: titles are computed directly from the prompt text rather than asking the model to generate a title, trading a punchier title for zero added latency and cost; the option to switch to an AI-generated title later was explicitly left open.
[2026-07-22T03:28:24.515Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=4fdef5ef13c82a0ab42e20e8b21a372c] Topic: Provision backend storage bucket and columns for project thumbnails
[2026-07-22T03:28:24.515Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=4fdef5ef13c82a0ab42e20e8b21a372c]   Trigger:   Saving and displaying thumbnails required new backend resources — a storage location for the images and new database columns — that couldn't be created from the app's normal user-level access.
[2026-07-22T03:28:24.515Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=4fdef5ef13c82a0ab42e20e8b21a372c]   Response:  - Documented the required one-time setup in a new setup guide: creating a public storage bucket named for thumbnails, and adding `thumbnail_url`/`thumbnail_key` columns to the projects table via a migration.
- Noted that the existing owner-only update policy on the projects table already covers writing these new columns, with a fallback policy snippet provided in case that policy doesn't yet exist.
[2026-07-22T03:28:24.515Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=4fdef5ef13c82a0ab42e20e8b21a372c]   Decisions: Followed the same "document required backend setup separately" pattern already established for a prior Shopify export feature, since the CLI needed to provision these resources wasn't available in this environment — this keeps the setup reproducible via CLI or dashboard SQL without blocking app-code delivery.
[2026-07-22T03:28:24.515Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=4fdef5ef13c82a0ab42e20e8b21a372c] Topic: Fix silent thumbnail failures and backfill missing previews for older projects
[2026-07-22T03:28:24.515Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=4fdef5ef13c82a0ab42e20e8b21a372c]   Trigger:   The user reported that project cards weren't showing thumbnails, even though the feature had just been implemented.
[2026-07-22T03:28:24.515Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=4fdef5ef13c82a0ab42e20e8b21a372c]   Response:  - Diagnosed two causes: projects created before this feature never triggered any capture, and all capture/upload errors were being silently discarded, so there was no visibility into whether the backend setup was missing or something else was broken.
- Added a lazy backfill (`ensureProjectThumbnail`) that runs when the Projects page loads: for any project without a thumbnail, it loads that project's saved pages and theme, renders the preview page offscreen, captures it, and updates the card live as each one resolves sequentially.
- Replaced silent failure handling with explicit console warnings that name the exact failure stage (render, upload, public-url resolution, or save) and point to the setup documentation, to make root-causing future issues immediate.
[2026-07-22T03:28:24.515Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=4fdef5ef13c82a0ab42e20e8b21a372c]   Decisions: - **Sequential backfill over parallel**: thumbnails for existing projects are generated one at a time rather than all at once, trading some speed for avoiding a burst of simultaneous offscreen renders that could hog the browser's main thread.
- **Surface errors via console warnings rather than UI alerts**: failures are logged with enough detail to diagnose (which stage failed, pointer to setup docs) without adding user-facing error UI, since capture is inherently best-effort and non-critical to the user's workflow.
[2026-07-22T03:28:24.515Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=4fdef5ef13c82a0ab42e20e8b21a372c]   Todo:      Waiting on user confirmation of whether the storage bucket and database columns have been provisioned, and on console warning output, to pinpoint whether remaining failures are a setup issue or a render/upload bug.
