[2026-07-22T13:51:13.157Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c2f53ed61d3bc230f0643edd718cc553] Topic: Require sign-in before opening Projects or Billing, but keep Home public
[2026-07-22T13:51:13.157Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c2f53ed61d3bc230f0643edd718cc553]   Trigger:   The user asked that anyone who is not signed in and tries to open the Projects or Billing page be sent to the sign-in page first, then quickly followed up to make sure the Home page stays reachable without signing in.
[2026-07-22T13:51:13.157Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c2f53ed61d3bc230f0643edd718cc553]   Response:  - Added a shared authentication check (`components/AppAuthGate.tsx`) wrapped around the authenticated app layout (`app/(app)/layout.tsx`), so it runs once for every page inside that section instead of being duplicated per page.
- The gate treats the root path as public and lets it render immediately, while any other path under the authenticated section blocks rendering and redirects unauthenticated visitors to `/sign-in` with the originally-requested path attached as a `next` parameter.
- Removed the now-redundant client-side redirect logic from `app/(app)/billing/page.tsx` and `app/(app)/projects/page.tsx`, and updated `app/(auth)/sign-in/page.tsx` to read the `next` parameter and send the user back to the page they originally tried to open after a successful login.
[2026-07-22T13:51:13.157Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=c2f53ed61d3bc230f0643edd718cc553]   Decisions: - **Centralized gate over per-page checks**: instead of repeating the sign-in redirect logic on each protected page, the check was moved into the shared layout so Projects, Billing, and any future protected page behave consistently and content never briefly flashes before the redirect happens.
- **Explicit public-route exception**: rather than removing the gate or scoping it more narrowly by route group, the Home page was explicitly excluded from the check so it stays open while everything else in the same layout remains protected.
- **Return-to-original-page after login**: the sign-in flow was extended to honor a return path so users who get redirected are dropped back on the page they wanted, rather than always landing on the homepage after signing in.
